  "body": "### Description\r\n\r\nI know it's entirely my fault, but I lost access to my HS's sqlite db when transitioning to psql on a re-instanced VPS, and now my domain is almost unusable. I know it's not an issue, but I'd like to kindly relay Maximus's advice from over in the support room to make the docs clearer about this peculiarity, and ask for a way to track any future progress should there ever be a solution for this.\r\n\r\nThank you very much and sorry for the noise.\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\nInstall, install psql without migrating the db [I know, I know]\r\n\r\nAll hell breaks loose: https://hastebin.com/tofuvifebu.pl\r\n\r\n### Version information\r\n\r\n- **Homeserver**: Yes\r\n\r\n- **Version**:        Synapse/0.26.0\r\n\r\n- **Install method**: APT [https://www.digitalocean.com/community/tutorials/how-to-install-matrix-synapse-on-ubuntu-16-04]\r\n\r\n- **Platform**:       Ubuntu 16 VPS\r\n",
